# The vectors a reader fails when this rule is deleted, and no others:
# a nested object that refuses on its own latches rejected.
#
# CMakeLists.txt builds that reader, and ctest requires its failures to be
# exactly this list. A vector added to the corpus that pins the rule belongs here.
#
# The runner's object checks drive a callback that returns false against every
# refused vector in object.txt, so each of them goes red when the latch records
# nothing; the vectors the corpus states for the rule are the two object-callback
# ones.

object-callback-rejects
object-callback-rejects-is-terminal
object-refusal-propagates-out-of-the-nesting
object-refusal-past-the-end-propagates
object-wire-refusal-then-callback-rejects-keeps-past-end
object-wire-refusal-then-callback-rejects-keeps-nonzero-padding
